  _menuDescription: I don't bite
  _funFacts:
  - _fact: Ferrets sleep up to 18-20 hours a day and can enter a deep slumber so
      profound they appear limp and unresponsive, often causing owners to panic.
  - _fact: When extremely happy or excited, a ferret will puff out its tail, arch
      its back, and bounce around in an uncoordinated, frantic display of pure joy.
  - _fact: Because of ferrets long, tubular bodies, ferrets were historically trained
      to run cables through tight spaces. They famously ran wires for the wedding
      of Prince Charles and Princess Diana.
  - _fact: Ferrets have poor eyesight but an incredibly sharp sense of smell, recognizing
      their owners by scent rather than by face.
